      "Language": "ger",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "High cholesterol values enhance the development of coronary heart disease. Therefore they must be normalized within the framework of a primary and secondary prevention. Apart from the risk factor cholesterol, other influencable and non-influencencable risk factors play a decisive role for the patient concerned. The simultaneous presence of these factors also finally determines the intensity of the lipid-lowering therapy. For a successful therapy, besides dietary measures, modern therapeutic drugs are available, and their use--as a rule--helps to normalize moderate and strongly increased cholesterol values. Despite all help in decision-making it always will remain the decision of a responsible doctor, which measures he will take to reduce the individual coronary risk of a particular patient entrusted to him."},
